Catalog tools are offline in this session, so here is the program built from the source text, checked against the authoring rules (unique stepIds, sequential chains per track, a `resourceConstraint` for every task, no hand-copied repetition).

Structure: the pork owns the smoker from t=0; trim/rub rides in its own track so cook 2 rubs while the smoker heats; beans and slaw both fire when the shoulder goes **into** the cooler (`afterStep … event: "start"`); the kettle is delayed with `programStartOffset` so the grill chain lands exactly as the pork is pulled; the final "lay it all out" is a `compound`/"all" barrier that waits on both the table set-out and the pulled pork. Planning durations converge everything on 12h00m.

- Smoker: light 0–45 · bark 45–405 · wrap 405–415 · wrapped 415–595 · cooler 595–685 · pull 685–715
- Beans (side burner): 595–607 fry → simmer 607–720 (indefinite, "until you serve", default 113m)
- Slaw: 595–615 shred · 615–623 dressing · 623–720 chill (fridge, ≥45m)
- Kettle (offset 653m): light 653–678 · sausages 678–692 · corn 692–702 · buns 702–705 · set out 705–715
- Lay out 715–720 — everything on the table together.
- Binding constraint: the offset smoker (the kettle offset is derived from it); `prep` peaks at exactly 2 concurrent (pull + set-out), matching the two cooks.

